item.description:
 &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;1-Associative-thinking&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#1-Associative-thinking&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;1. Associative thinking&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;1. Associative thinking&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;The first creative method is associative thinking. This is a method everyone uses more or less unconsciously when thinking. It’s a bit like brainstorming: you take a core thing as a starting point, associate the elements related to it, and extend outward in a radial way. Thinking by association sounds like a very simple method, but most of the time thoughts race around in the brain in a messy, disordered and illogical way, so we need some systematic methods to settle our thinking down and find a clear direction for our ideas. If you don’t know where to start, we can think from three directions: horizontal association, vertical association and relational association. Horizontal association &lt;strong&gt;means diverging around the core thing, only considering things directly related to the core thing, that is, things associated at one degree of separation.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span id=&#34;more&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi1.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi1&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Horizontal association. For example, let’s do an exercise: name 10 things related to “wind”. You might think of “cold, winter, desert, seaside, leaves, kite, long hair, dust, silk scarf, air” and so on. These are all things directly related to “wind”. If horizontal association is drawing a circle around a point, then we can also make its radius bigger and do vertical association. &lt;strong&gt;Starting from the core thing, each associated thing must be related to the previous thing, digging deeper to find things associated with the core thing at two, three, even five or six degrees of separation.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi2.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi2&#34;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vertical association. For example, still using “wind” as the theme for vertical association, we can think of “wind — kite — spring — willow — buds — catkins — seeds — life” and so on. In addition, we can also associate from the angle of relatedness, associating what two things have in common. This is very useful for designs with more than one theme. For example, name 10 things “wind” and “fire” have in common. We can think of wind and fire both being “formless, destructive, able to produce energy, untouchable, something you can feel, natural, able to be produced artificially, air, able to be big or small, hard to control”. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyyi3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyyi3&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Relational association. Through association in these three directions, we can diverge creatively as much as we like.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;2-Diverge-and-converge&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#2-Diverge-and-converge&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;2. Diverge and converge&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;2. Diverge and converge&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;The diverge-and-converge method is actually a way of thinking that can be applied anywhere. &lt;strong&gt;First diverge on your own, then screen the possibilities, and finally converge on a solid direction.&lt;/strong&gt; By repeatedly alternating “diverging — proposing creative ideas” and “converging — analyzing and screening creative ideas”, you gradually reach the expected goal. For example, in design, &lt;strong&gt;we can first list all possible creative points, then analyze and screen out the feasible ideas, then diverge again and raise the problems that need to be solved in that idea, then converge again and focus on the best solution, alternating back and forth like this until the goal is finally reached.&lt;/strong&gt; With this funnel-shaped way of thinking, the ideas that finally settle out have all been screened layer by layer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi4.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi4&#34;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;3-Mapping-reality&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#3-Mapping-reality&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;3. Mapping reality&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;3. Mapping reality&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;When people talk about mapping reality, many think of skeuomorphic design. The original skeuomorphic design was meant to lower the user’s learning cost and guide correct operation. However, as people use electronic products more and more, their acceptance of virtual interfaces is getting higher and higher; without the guidance of skeuomorphism, users still know how to operate things. Some skeuomorphic interfaces overemphasize details, which also places a visual and cognitive burden on users. But drawing inspiration from the real world doesn’t mean you must 100% reproduce the real texture of the physical world. What you distill and abstract from reality can be form, color, texture, or movement patterns, optical and mechanical properties, and other parts that are most characteristic of an object. For example, the design style of Google Material Design was inspired by paper and ink. By simplifying complex visual elements like this, you can likewise design products that are both simple and able to stir users’ emotions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi5.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi5&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Mapping reality. Take the example below: the iOS 6 weather forecast interface has a strong texture, and the glass panel effect and the details of the weather icons completely simulate real things. Looking at it now, the visual style seems a bit outdated. The second image is the iOS 7 weather forecast, which removes the strong texture and the visual burden; we feel its information is presented more clearly and it emphasizes content more, which is a good design — but would you say it’s special or moving? Probably not. Now look at the interface of a third weather app, Haze. Haze reflects how temperature feels through changes in color; from 34° to 37° the color gradually deepens and becomes more vivid, and you feel hotter and hotter. The direction in which the background ripples float reflects the trend of temperature change, and the amplitude of the ripples shows whether the temperature difference is large or small — a big temperature difference makes it float quickly, a small one makes it float only slightly. Whether it’s color or the trend of change, these are in fact characteristics abstracted from reality, truthfully reproducing the way temperature feels, and a design like this makes people feel it is full of emotion and is moving. These are all inspirations reality gives us.&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chunagyi6.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chunagyi6&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Three weather app designs. Now look at Paper’s interface: the card-style design looks flat, but it actually carries a metaphor, an operational hint that comes from real-world logic — we can touch, flip and rotate these “cards”, and the cards won’t disappear out of nowhere but move along with the user. What looks like a flat design is in fact also a kind of mapping and abstraction of the “real world”.&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi7.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi7&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;4-Combining-elements&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#4-Combining-elements&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;4. Combining elements&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;4. Combining elements&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;In nature, elements can be combined to form all kinds of new substances — for example, hydrogen and oxygen can become water. Combining different old elements in new ways can also produce new ideas. Combining elements is not simply stacking them either; it can be seen as a kind of creation built on top of what already exists.&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi8.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi8&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;For example, a pencil with an eraser looks like nothing more than an ordinary thing now, but when an American painter invented that pencil, the patent sold for 550,000 US dollars and was regarded as a great creation — in fact it was just the result of stacking elements. The Walkman was rated one of the great music inventions of the past 50 years, and it too was the stacking of headphones + a recorder. As shown below, Flappy Bird and 2048 are two mini games with completely different controls, yet the game designer cleverly stacked the two together and it became a new hit mini game.&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi9.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi9&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Next let’s look at two Durex marketing cases. A hit 2048 mini game, combined with Durex’s usage scenarios — single, chatting someone up, dating, falling in love, hugging, kissing and so on, until the final stage where Durex is used — became a highly shareable marketing case. Durex never tires of this trick: its “N times a night” mini game is old wine in a new bottle too, using the format of the hit game “Don’t Guess the Black Block”, which lets everyone play it right away, and the slightly risqué spoof copy makes people very happy to share it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chunagyi10.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chunagyi10&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Two of Durex’s marketing mini games. From those two cases we can see that it’s really just a product’s core function fused with a classic or trendy mini game, and it becomes a New Idea. The product’s core function is Durex’s usage scenarios, plus 2048, Don’t Guess the Black Block, or widely spread mini games like Plane Shooting or Crazy Guess the Picture; and in the end, because it’s simple and easy to pick up and a bit of off-color fun, it becomes a highly spreadable marketing plan.&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi11.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi11&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Author: @ME NetEase Mobile Design Source: &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.uisdc.com/4-way-become-creative-designer&#34;&gt;UISDC&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;1、联想思维&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#1、联想思维&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;1、联想思维&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;1、联想思维&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;第一个创意方法，就是联想思维。这是每个人在思考时都会潜移默化使用到的一个方法。有点像头脑风暴，以一个核心事物为起点，将与之有关的元素进行联 想，以一种放射性的方式向外延展。思维联想听起来是个很简单的方法，但是大多数时候，思维在大脑中流窜，是杂乱无序、没有逻辑的，所以我们需要一些系统化 的方法将思维沉淀下来，为思路找一个清晰的方向。如果不知道从哪里入手，我们可以从三方向进行思考：横向联想、纵向联想和关联联想。 横向联想是&lt;strong&gt;指围绕核心事物进行发散，只考虑与核心事物有直接关联的，也就是一度关联的事物。&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span id=&#34;more&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi1.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi1&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;横向联想 比如我们做个练习，说出与“风”相关的10件事物。大家也许可以想到“寒冷、冬天、沙漠、海边、树叶、风筝、长发、尘土、丝巾、空气”等等。这些都是与“风”直接相关的事物。 如果说横向联想是在一个点周围画了一个圈，那么我们还可以使它的半径变大，进行纵向联想。&lt;strong&gt;从核心事物开始，联想的后一样事物要与前一样事物有关联，深挖下去，找到与核心事物有二度、三度、甚至五度、六度关联的事物。&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi2.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi2&#34;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;纵向联想 比如，还是以“风”为主题进行纵向联想，我们可以想到“风——风筝——春天——柳树——枝芽——飞絮——种子——生命”等等。 除此之外，我们还可以从关联性这个角度进行联想，联想两两事物之间的共同之处。这对于主题不仅一个的设计是很有用的。比如说出“风”与“火”的10 个共通之处。我们可以想到风与火都是“无形、有破坏力、可以产生能量、摸不到、可以感受到、自然、 可以人为产生、空气、可大可小、难以控制的”。 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyyi3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyyi3&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;关联联想 通过这三个方向的联想，我们可以尽情的发散创意。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;2、发散聚敛&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#2、发散聚敛&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;2、发散聚敛&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;2、发散聚敛&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;发散聚敛法，其实这是一种可以应用在任何地方的思维方式，&lt;strong&gt;先自我发散，再筛选可能，最后聚合成一个靠谱的方向。&lt;/strong&gt;通过“发散——提出创造性设想”和“聚敛——对创造性设想进行分析筛选”的反复交叉进行，逐步达到预期目标。 比如在设计中，&lt;strong&gt;我们可以先列举所有可能的创意点，然后分析筛选出可行的创意，然后再发散，提出这个创意中需要解决的问题，再聚敛，聚焦到那个最好的解决办法，如此反复交替进行，最终达到目标。&lt;/strong&gt; 这种漏斗型的思维方式，最后沉淀下来的想法，都是经过层层筛选的。&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi4.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi4&#34;&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;3、现实映射&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#3、现实映射&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;3、现实映射&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;3、现实映射&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;提到现实映射，很多人会想到拟物化的设计，最初的拟物化设计是为了减低用户的学习成本，引导正确操作。然而随着人们越来越多的使用电子产品，对于虚 拟界面的接受程度也越来越高，不需要拟物化的引导，用户也知道应该如何操作。有些拟物化界面过于强调细节，也给用户造成了视觉和认知的负担。 但其实从现实世界借鉴灵感并不意味着一定要100%还原物理世界的真实质感， 从现实中提炼、抽象出的，可以是形态、色彩、质感，也可以是运动方式、光学力学特性等物体中最有特征的部分。比如Google Material Design的设计风格，灵感就来源于纸张和墨水。像这样将繁复的视觉元素进行简化处理，一样可以设计出既简约又可以调动起用户情感的产品。&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi5.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi5&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;现实映射 如下图这个例子，iOS 6的天气预报界面，质感比较强烈，玻璃板的效果和天气图标的细节，完全模拟现实事物。现在看来，视觉风格有那么一点点过时。第二张图是iOS 7的天气预报，去掉了强烈的质感，没有了视觉负担，我们会觉得它的信息展现更加清楚，更加强调内容，是个不错的设计，可是你会觉得它很特别、打动人心吗？ 好像都没有。再来看第三个天气app Haze的界面。Haze以颜色的变化反映出温度给人的感觉，从34°到37°，颜色是逐渐加深，变艳丽的，你会感觉越来越热。以背景波纹的浮动方向，反 应出温度的变化趋势，以波纹变化幅度表明温度差是大还是小，温差大就浮动的很快，温差小就浮动得很小，无论是颜色还是变化趋势，其实都是从现实中抽象出的 特点，真实的还原出温度给人的那种感觉，这样的设计更会让人觉得饱含情感，打动人心。这些都是现实给我们的灵感。&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chunagyi6.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chunagyi6&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;三款天气App设计 再来看Paper的界面，卡片式的设计看起来是扁平的，其实也带有一种隐喻，有一种来自现实逻辑的操作暗示：我们可以去摸、去翻动、去旋转这些“卡片”， 这些卡片不会凭空消失，而是随着用户的移动而移动。 看似扁平的设计，实际也是对“真实世界”的一种映射和抽象。&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi7.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi7&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;4、元素组合&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#4、元素组合&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;4、元素组合&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;4、元素组合&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;在自然界，元素可以通过组合形成各种各样的新物质，比如氢气和氧气可以变成水。将不同的旧元素进行新的叠加组合，也可以产生新的创意。元素的组合也不是简单的叠加，可以看做是在原有基础上的一种创造。&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi8.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi8&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;比如带着橡皮的铅笔，现在看起来是在普通不过的一种东西，但是当一个美国画家发明这种铅笔的时候，这项专利就卖了55万美元，被看做是一个伟大的创造，其实这就是元素叠加的结果。随身听被评为过去50年来伟大的音乐发明，其实它也是耳机+录音机的叠加。 如下图所示，Flappy Bird和2048是操作完全不同的两款小游戏，可游戏设计师却能巧妙的将两者叠加在一起，变成了新的热门小游戏。&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi9.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi9&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;下面一起来看两个杜蕾斯的营销案例。一款热门的2048小游戏，结合杜蕾斯的使用场景，单身-搭讪-约会-恋爱-拥抱-接吻等等，直到最后用到杜蕾斯的那个环节，变成了一个很有传播性的营销案例。 杜蕾斯用这招屡试不爽，一夜N次郎的小游戏同样是老壶装新酒，用的是热门游戏别猜黑块的形式，让大家一看就会玩，而且略有重口味的恶搞文案让大家很乐于去分享。&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chunagyi10.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chunagyi10&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;杜蕾斯的两个营销小游戏 从刚才那两个案例中我们看到，其实就是一个产品的核心功能，融合上一个或经典或流行的小游戏，就变成了一个New Idea，产品核心功能就是杜蕾斯的使用场景，加上2048，别猜黑块，或者是像打飞机、疯狂猜图这种传播很广的小游戏，最终因为它简单易上手，又有点恶 趣味，成为了很有传播性的营销方案。&lt;br&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://image.woshipm.com/wp-files/2015/04/chuangyi11.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;chuangyi11&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;作者：@ME网易移动设计 来源：&lt;a href=&#34;http://www.uisdc.com/4-way-become-creative-designer&#34;&gt;优设网&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;p&gt;It’s dark now, the night has grown drunk…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time returns to before 2014. Bright eyes flicker across the sky now and then; I linger in the sweet rain I never tire of tasting, slowly savoring these early-morning hours…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On campus, the dark-green lawn heaves and wanders with an indescribable heaviness, silently fading. I am here, reveling boundlessly in emotions that rise and fall again and again. Sometimes I feel that the decay of time is a punishment for life — only because I refuse the outside, refuse to slip…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mystery that has cut off the sunlight wears a childhood smile in its gaps, unknowing, unwilling. Layer upon layer of woolly snow steeped in the sky is the rampage of early-spring fibers; this has gone beyond my awareness, and I even feel a certain awe before life. Perceive the world you know, sense the realm you wish to reach, drift in the breathing of the wind all around…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I am here; this place holds so much love. I am here — thank goodness I am already here. Farewell, that world of mine: the astringent-sweet spring water, the furious discontent, the age of shouting, ending me and my world. And now, more than six years on, never to return again…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No more, never more; not much time remains. In truth, the almonds of the North are very bitter — astringently bitter…&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;p&gt;天黑了，夜色醉了…… &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;时间重新回到2014年之前。天上不时有闪过明眸，我呆在尝尝未甘霖的雨露里慢慢享受着清晨着些……&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;校园上，暗绿色的草坪，起伏游荡有种说不出的沉重，默默逝色。我在，看着反复起落的情绪中陶醉无边。有时甚觉时间的颓败是一种生命的惩罚，只因我拒绝外在，拒绝失误……&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;断了阳光的玄子，间隙上插着儿时的微笑，不明间，不然已。一层层泡在天空的毛雪，是初春纤维的肆虐，这已出乎我的觉察，竟有些敬畏生命。感知你所知道的世界，觉察你所想达到的境界，淌洋于四周风的呼吸……&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;我在，这地方有如此多的爱。我在，还好我已经在。 别了，我的那个世界，涩甜的泉水，愤怒的不满，吼叫时代，终结着我和我的世界。而今6年有余，不曾再会回归……&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;不再，永不在，尚存已不多时日。 其实，北方的杏仁很苦，涩涩的苦……&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://www.dgtle.com/home.php?mod=space&amp;amp;uid=7589&amp;amp;do=profile&#34;&gt;陈繁leon&lt;/a&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Foreword · The bar for budget phones rises:&lt;/strong&gt; Budget phones have arguably been the volume-driving weapon of recent years, with a new model appearing almost every month. If it isn’t Lenovo launching a 599-yuan phone last month, it’s Meizu releasing the 999-yuan Meilan this month, or Redmi getting its next generation refresh the month after. Manufacturers seem tireless at the thousand-yuan tier, but because of the price limits, today’s budget phones are not all that different from one another. Consumers are getting more and more rational, and now that budget phones barely differ, getting users to choose ours means we have to be far better than the competition in some respect. And the thousand-yuan segment is iterating too, making every detail better: the most visible upgrades this year are 1080P screens, 4G, bigger storage, 3000mAh large batteries and so on.&lt;span id=&#34;more&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/144406tujmmp7ou4zam51a.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;21.jpg&#34; title=&#34;21.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/144236q4v369ece9t41g43.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;22.jpg&#34; title=&#34;22.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TCL also launched the 么么哒 3N (M2M) not long ago. Speaking of 么么哒 phones, I’m sure everyone is familiar with them — this is a brand-new brand that only launched at the end of March this year. The name “么么哒” is very fresh and cute, it feels more intimate and more human, and it leaves a deep impression. The TCL 么么哒 3N basically pushes the thousand-yuan spec sheet to the top: a MediaTek MT6752 true octa-core 64-bit processor, 2GB RAM + 16GB ROM, a 5.5-inch 1080P screen, and a built-in 3500mAh battery. Of course it supports the China Mobile 4G version, dual SIM dual standby, and memory expansion is a given too, yet the price is only 899 yuan. So how does the experience hold up after all that hardware upgrading? Let’s take a look:&lt;strong&gt;Design · Faux brushed metal finish:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004254owwh5qhwxaqeocf5.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;2.jpg&#34; title=&#34;2.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have seen a 么么哒 phone before, you will probably be a little disappointed by the new model’s looks, because overall it isn’t much different from its predecessor. If you insist on finding a big difference, it’s that the body’s four sides are now curved and more rounded, a little less stern and a little more soft, and that the color lineup uses champagne gold for the first time. The TCL 么么哒 3N measures 152.3 *76.4 * 7.95mm, and although it is less than 8mm thick, it still feels a bit big in the hand.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004238wwvx5i8xdofxopdz.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;1.jpg&#34; title=&#34;1.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/005045mxyv4dv5x3vgd1fy.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;8.jpg&#34; title=&#34;8.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For the screen, the TCL 么么哒 3N abandons the 720P panel that users so disliked on big screens, and instead uses a 5.5-inch 1080P HD screen that is very rare at the budget tier, with a pixel density of 401PPI and OGS full-lamination, so the display is very clear and sharp, and the color temperature is fairly neutral as well. The “resting screen aesthetics” are done well too: on standby, it’s hard to tell where the screen ends and the bezel begins on the front of the TCL 么么哒 3N, which looks very pretty.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/005416ayylvxx4244hzoho.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;12.jpg&#34; title=&#34;12.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004302kk3yqmzmjhyrtajw.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;3.jpg&#34; title=&#34;3.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Up top there’s still the earpiece and the front camera, and the three traditional capacitive keys below the screen look especially large. Unfortunately they aren’t backlit, though there seem to be few breathing-light keys at the thousand-yuan tier, so the manufacturer apparently felt this was money it could save.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004709i6rfzdcqt3vr3cl3.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;7.jpg&#34; title=&#34;7.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The back cover of the TCL 么么哒 3N is made of polycarbonate plastic, and the champagne-colored cover in Fanfan’s hands has a subtle brushed-metal texture, throwing off slivers of light when it reflects, and because it is understated it doesn’t feel nouveau riche. This material isn’t slip-resistant, but it doesn’t easily pick up fingerprints, so friends with oily hands can handle it easily too.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004332hw14rkhvvho3rddg.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;6.jpg&#34; title=&#34;6.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/005405zhudrwrvezebqdl6.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;11.jpg&#34; title=&#34;11.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The TCL 么么哒 N3 uses a 13-megapixel camera, and you can see a silver decorative ring around the camera, which is definitely a visual plus. The TCL logo is printed below the LED flash, and the loudspeaker sits at the bottom of the body. The speaker is a horizontal long-row speaker with very densely packed holes, and the dots on either side do a good job of preventing the volume from being muffled when the phone is set down on a desk, preserving the speaker’s volume as much as possible.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/005122uco74pgggp1rj24d.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;10.jpg&#34; title=&#34;10.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/005113ms4qanpwzw8i004k.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;9.jpg&#34; title=&#34;9.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004318n31a1z1wlep6babw.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;5.jpg&#34; title=&#34;5.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The phone’s frame also uses a brushed-metal finish, creating a metallic feel on a plastic body. Of course the texture is different, but we also don’t need to worry about metal affecting the signal. The side buttons are distributed fairly sensibly: the left side is left empty, while the volume key, power key and other physical buttons are all on the right side. The physical keys are well placed — your finger reaches them without any strain — and the key feedback is full and firm. A 3.5mm headphone jack and the charging port sit at the top and bottom of the body respectively.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004308b2vfgfofbmfc3cbv.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;4.jpg&#34; title=&#34;4.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The TCL 么么哒 N3 uses a unibody design. Usually opening the SIM tray on a unibody phone requires a SIM pin, but the TCL 么么哒 3N’s tray is more user-friendly: no pin needed, just press the bump on the tray cover. The tray is a pop-out design — we simply press down on the “bump” end to open it. The tray also seals nicely; when closed it effectively keeps out light splashes and dust. There are still plenty of small problems in use though — for example, the tray sits quite deep, so if you don’t have fingernails or a sharp object to help press it, pulling the SIM card in and out becomes very difficult. On the plus side, the TCL 么么哒 3N supports TD-LTE dual SIM dual standby, which everyone probably knows by now, and both card slots support China Mobile’s 4G network, with no distinction between primary and secondary — either one can activate 4G data.&lt;strong&gt;System · Lewa-flavored 么么哒 2.0:&lt;/strong&gt;The TCL 么么哒 N3’s ROM is a collaboration with the third party 乐蛙, using 乐蛙OS 5.1, a deeply customized system based on Android 4.4. Anyone who plays with phones is surely familiar with 乐蛙OS; it’s good in both looks and functionality, and counts as one of the better Chinese ROMs. 乐蛙OS 5.1 can’t really be called fully flat — it sits somewhere between skeuomorphic and flat, and the icons look a bit large and slightly out of proportion, but none of this hurts the user experience. The 乐蛙OS style is actually quite ingratiating: fresh, natural and clean overall, with soft fonts, and after turning on large fonts, older users should be quite fond of it. &lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143323jh857n88zu5ayya6.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;13.jpg&#34; title=&#34;13.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;乐蛙OS 5.1 is quite practical when it comes to off-screen gestures and smart motion sensing. For example: besides double-tapping to wake the screen, it also supports writing letters on the screen while it’s off to quickly launch the corresponding app. Fanfan tried it a few times and it worked well — bundled apps respond fairly quickly, while third-party apps are noticeably slower. Smart motion sensing is mostly about “air gestures”: we can complete the corresponding operations without touching the screen, for example sweeping a palm across the screen while it’s on to unlock it.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143356bqxuzqngs4znfdtf.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;15.jpg&#34; title=&#34;15.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The TCL 么么哒 3N integrates T-show, a new news aggregation page with an all-new “waterfall” layout. Swipe left from the home screen to wake it; it presents trending content in waterfall-style tiles and lets you pick the categories you like. It’s light reading — read it whenever and wherever you want. All of the content comes from highlights around the web, curated and pushed to everyone. Of course, once you’ve developed particular reading interests, the TCL 么么哒 3N will automatically push related content based on your preferences, and the content is updated fairly frequently.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143339r96scs50ob6sp9ib.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;14.jpg&#34; title=&#34;14.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The TCL 么么哒 3N has another very nice feature — 么么哒 2.0, which lets you transfer files between phone and phone, or phone and computer, with zero data usage. The app shares the phone’s name, “么么哒”, which is perhaps where the phone got its name. Simply put two phones with the 么么哒 app installed on the same network segment and data transfer is done; it supports any type of file, and can even transfer already-installed apps. Free from the shackles of a data cable, for lazy people like us it couldn’t be more practical. In addition, 么么哒 2.0 also supports connecting to Apple devices and computers.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143508baw9h0whnj2kroah.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;18.jpg&#34; title=&#34;18.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The TCL 么么哒 3N comes with a security center that provides virus protection, security blocking, junk cleaning, auto-start management and notification management, solving messy app problems for users in one go. It also provides a power-saving management system that can automatically run smart power-saving, best used while you sleep at night; with a large battery plus a decent power-saving system, it brings us a longer battery life experience.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143533blmvvmljm37v5jlf.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;19.jpg&#34; title=&#34;19.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In fact, the TCL 么么哒 3N brings a great many nice little features as well, such as color temperature adjustment so we don’t fear warm or cool screens, and a Messages icon that occasionally wriggles like jelly when there are new texts.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143601gqfxim7iie77r9wc.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;20.jpg&#34; title=&#34;20.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance · Strong octa-core with solid battery life:&lt;/strong&gt; Hardware strength is a very important point for budget phones — you need decent performance at a low price, and thankfully MediaTek is there to handle that. Although the TCL 么么哒 3N doesn’t have luxurious hardware like a Snapdragon 805, it has upgrades across screen, processor, memory and storage. The TCL 么么哒 3N carries a 64-bit MediaTek MT6752 octa-core processor clocked up to 1.7GHz. Running memory is upgraded to 2GB and body storage is raised to 16GB as well. That’s a pretty good configuration for the price: it keeps the system running smoothly while leaving enough storage headroom for multitasking. Judging by actual benchmark results, it really surprised me a bit — it hit a high score of 40000+ on AnTuTu. &lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143440l17u5u4swohor3ss.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;17.jpg&#34; title=&#34;17.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond those benchmark numbers, I also tried a few games on the TCL 么么哒 3N. Asphalt 8 ran very smoothly, with no crashes or screen ghosting along the way. But when I tried Fish Hunter 3, the wallpaper behind everything went black — a bug. MediaTek processors still have compatibility problems in some games.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143413w2eqvq7c2w2ek21e.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;16.jpg&#34; title=&#34;16.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On battery life, the TCL 么么哒 3N has a built-in 3500mAh battery, a capacity that already exceeds the standard of most budget phones today — plenty of flagships don’t have one this big either. In actual use, two days of everyday use should be no problem at all.&lt;strong&gt;Camera · Decent by day, needs work at night:&lt;/strong&gt;The TCL 么么哒 3N uses an 8MP front camera and a Sony 13MP IMX214 stacked rear camera. In the shooting interface, besides the usual filter effects, HDR and panorama, you can also manually adjust exposure compensation, white balance and other parameters. The interface looks a bit dated and could use more design effort in the future. &lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152224jvgu9gixu1qxxuqb.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;31.jpg&#34; title=&#34;31.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/151912rnhe2f3qienh37f7.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;25.jpg&#34; title=&#34;25.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The TCL 么么哒 3N’s daytime imaging is pretty good. The overall saturation of the photos is nice and the color reproduction is fairly true. In some scenes with large differences in lighting there is smearing, while white balance control in big scenes is passable.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/151848n1m6zmyr9d7qmmk1.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;24.jpg&#34; title=&#34;24.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/151941ppp0vhfqo7gyloc0.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;26.jpg&#34; title=&#34;26.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Focus speed is on the slow side in macro shots, and it occasionally focuses inaccurately — though it’s certainly much better than the 599-yuan Lenovo Lemon.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152330q4txomtgxcxxcfct.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;27_副本.jpg&#34; title=&#34;27_副本.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152142ug9ccr4rb6hjrgr4.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;28.jpg&#34; title=&#34;28.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When shooting still objects, you can see that the image resolution is quite good, the color rendering is fairly true with high fidelity, and it looks full-bodied; the colors and exposure of the photos are just right.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152204p6u42dp69j44huux.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;30.jpg&#34; title=&#34;30.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152116u9mehf9v2raumroa.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;29.jpg&#34; title=&#34;29.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Noise control and color reproduction at night fall a bit short, and both noise suppression and glare handling need further work.&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/150627ap5fgp46k9agi9iu.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;23.jpg&#34; title=&#34;23.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For selfies, the front camera is a full 8MP, so it can take high-quality selfies, and paired with beauty mode it’s pretty good.&lt;strong&gt;Conclusion · Flawed but still a bargain:&lt;/strong&gt;Taken as a whole, the TCL 么么哒 3N really can be said to set a new benchmark for budget phone hardware. In terms of design the 么么哒 3N is still fairly conservative, but it blends in fashionable color combinations so the whole device doesn’t feel cheap. The system leaves a so-so impression but is still very solid and practical. On the hardware side, the 1080P HD screen, octa-core 64-bit processor, 4G network, and 13MP Sony IMX214 camera all add a lot of points to the TCL 么么哒 3N. There’s also the very interesting 么么哒 2.0, which gives us a simpler way to transfer files. Of course the TCL 么么哒 3N still has plenty of problems, such as a SIM tray that sits too deep and less-than-ideal photo quality; these aren’t huge issues, but they still deserve attention. A phone priced under a thousand yuan really does live up to its price, and we needn’t nitpick over a budget phone — otherwise what would high-end phones be for? Right? &lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152313vkqnsrd11ozvvrqn.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;33.jpg&#34; title=&#34;33.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152244w8n3e8dm5nve85g8.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;32.jpg&#34; title=&#34;32.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pros:&lt;/strong&gt; 5.5-inch 1080P screen Both card slots support 4G 2GB RAM, 16GB storage 3500mAh battery&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cons:&lt;/strong&gt; MediaTek processor compatibility is average The card tray sits too deep, hard to swap cards System experience is lacking Photos are not ideal&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://www.dgtle.com/home.php?mod=space&amp;amp;uid=7589&amp;amp;do=profile&#34;&gt;陈繁leon&lt;/a&gt; &lt;strong&gt;前言 · 千元机门槛提升：&lt;/strong&gt; 千元机可以说是近年来充量的利器，几乎每个月都有新机。不是上个月联想发售599的新机，就是这个月魅族发售999魅蓝，还是下个月红米又要更新换代。似 乎厂商在千元级上都乐此不疲，但又由于价格限制，现在的千元机差异性不大。现在消费者越来越理性，千元机差异不大的今天，要让用户选择我们某方面要远比对 方出色。而现在千元就也进行着更替，把每个细节更加优秀，比如今年很显眼的升级就是屏幕升级1080P、4G、增加容量、3000毫安大电池等等。&lt;span id=&#34;more&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/144406tujmmp7ou4zam51a.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;21.jpg&#34; title=&#34;21.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/144236q4v369ece9t41g43.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;22.jpg&#34; title=&#34;22.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TCL前不久也发布了么么哒3N（M2M），说起么么哒手机，相信大家都不会陌生，这是今年款3月底才发布的全新品牌。“么么哒”这个名字非常小清新，感 觉更亲密，更人性化，让人印象深刻。TCL么么哒3N  基本上把千元的配置达到了顶级，联发科MT6752真八核64位处理器，2GB RAM + 16GB ROM，采用5.5英寸1080P屏幕，内置3500mAh电池。当然支持移动4G 版本，双卡双待，内存扩展也是少不了的，但售价仅仅为899元，到底提升硬件以后体验如何呢？我们往下看：&lt;strong&gt;外观 · 仿金属拉丝工艺：&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004254owwh5qhwxaqeocf5.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;2.jpg&#34; title=&#34;2.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;如果你以前看过么么哒手机的话，应该会对新机的外观有些小失望，因为整体来看和前作差不太多。如果非要说有啥大差异，那就是机身四周经过了弧形处理更加圆 润，少了一分刚毅，多了一分柔美，而且在配色上首次使用香槟金。TCL么么哒3N 三围方面是152.3 *76.4 * 7.95mm，虽然厚度只有不到8mm，拿在手上还是有些大的。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004238wwvx5i8xdofxopdz.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;1.jpg&#34; title=&#34;1.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/005045mxyv4dv5x3vgd1fy.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;8.jpg&#34; title=&#34;8.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TCL么么哒3N 在屏幕放弃了在大屏上饱受用户嫌弃的720P屏幕，而采用千元机领域里十分罕见的5.5 寸1080P高清屏，像素密度达到了401PPI，并采用 OGS全贴合工艺，显示效果非常清晰锐利，同时在色温上也比较中和。息屏美学方面也做的不错，在待机的状态下，TCL么么哒3N 正面看上去很难区分屏幕与边框的界限，非常有美感。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/005416ayylvxx4244hzoho.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;12.jpg&#34; title=&#34;12.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004302kk3yqmzmjhyrtajw.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;3.jpg&#34; title=&#34;3.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;屏幕上面还是听筒和前置摄像头，下方的三颗传统的触控按键显得格外大，可惜不支持背光呼吸灯，不过目前千元级上貌似比较少有呼吸灯式按键，看来厂商觉得这是可以省下的钱。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004709i6rfzdcqt3vr3cl3.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;7.jpg&#34; title=&#34;7.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TCL么么哒3N 后盖采用了聚碳酸酯塑料做为机身材质，繁繁手中的香槟色后盖有着淡雅的金属拉丝质感，在光线反射下映射出一丝丝光芒，因为比较淡雅少一分土豪气。这种材质虽然不防滑但不容易留下指纹，手油的朋友们也可以轻松驾驭。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004332hw14rkhvvho3rddg.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;6.jpg&#34; title=&#34;6.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/005405zhudrwrvezebqdl6.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;11.jpg&#34; title=&#34;11.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TCL么么哒N3 采用了一颗1300万像素摄像头，可以看到摄像头周围采用了银色装饰圈，视觉上绝对是加分的。LED补光灯下方印有TCL 的LOGO，而外放扬声器放置在机身的底部。扬声器 采用横列式长排扬声器，开孔非常密集，两侧的圆点很好的避免手机放置在桌面时所造成的音量变小问题，最大程度上保证了扬声器的音量。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/005122uco74pgggp1rj24d.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;10.jpg&#34; title=&#34;10.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/005113ms4qanpwzw8i004k.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;9.jpg&#34; title=&#34;9.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004318n31a1z1wlep6babw.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;5.jpg&#34; title=&#34;5.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;手机的边框同样采用了金属拉丝工艺，在塑料的机身上塑造出了金属的质感，当然手感上是有差异的，但我们也不需要担心金属影响信号的问题。机身按键的分布还 是比较合理，左侧留空，音量键和电源键等实体按键都分布在机身右边。实体按键位置还不错，手指没有压力就可以触碰到，按键反馈力感十足，机身顶部和底部分 别分布着3.5mm耳机孔和充电接口。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/004308b2vfgfofbmfc3cbv.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;4.jpg&#34; title=&#34;4.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TCL么么哒N3 采用的是一体式机身，一般一体化机身的手机卡槽的开启往往需要借助卡针，而TCL么么哒3N卡槽比较人性化，无需任何卡针，轻触卡槽盖上的凸点即可打开。 这个卡槽是采用的弹出式的卡槽设计，我们只需轻轻按下“凸点”一端即可将卡槽开启，另外，卡槽的密闭性也很不错，关闭状态下能有效杜绝轻微水渍和灰尘。不 过使用还是有很多小问题，比如卡槽安放位置较深，如果没有指甲或者尖锐物品辅助按下的话，想要拔插SIM卡成为非常困难的事情。不错的是，TCL么么哒 3N 是支持TD-LTE双卡双待功能的，这个大家应该都知道，而且手机的两个卡槽均支持移动4G网络，并且不用区分主副卡，都能激活4G上网。&lt;strong&gt;系统 · 乐蛙加持么么达2.0：&lt;/strong&gt;TCL么么哒N3 在ROM方面是同第三方乐蛙合作，采用的是基于Android 4.4深度定制的乐蛙OS 5.1系统。乐蛙OS相信玩手机的朋友都不陌生吧，美观性与功能性都不错，算是国内比较优秀ROM的代表作之一。乐蛙OS 5.1并不能算是完全的扁平化，介于拟物化和扁平化之间，图标上显得有些大，有些不协调，但这些并没有影响使用体验。乐蛙OS的风格上其实还是比较讨好用 户的，整体感觉清新自然、干净，字体柔美，打开大字体后年长的用户应该比较偏爱。 &lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143323jh857n88zu5ayya6.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;13.jpg&#34; title=&#34;13.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;乐蛙OS 5.1 在息屏手势和智能体感方面还是比较实用的，比如：双击可以点亮屏幕外，还支持在息屏状态下在屏幕上写下字母快速启动相应程序，繁繁试了几次，还不错，自带 应用响应速度比较快，而第三方应用明显会慢一些。智能体感，更多的则是一些“隔空操作”，我们可以在不触碰屏幕就可以完成相应的功能操作，比如：亮屏状态 下手掌扫过屏幕即可解锁。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143356bqxuzqngs4znfdtf.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;15.jpg&#34; title=&#34;15.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TCL么么哒3N 整合了全新“瀑布流”的新闻聚合页面T-show杂志，在主屏幕状态下向左滑动即可唤醒，通过瀑布式方块展现时下热门内容，并可自行选择喜欢分类，属于轻 阅读，随时随地想看就看。上面的内容都是来源于网络上的精华内容，经过整合推送给大家。当然你养成了特定的阅读兴趣后，TCL么么哒3N 也会自动根据你的喜好推送相关内容给你，内容更新的频率也是比较高的。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143339r96scs50ob6sp9ib.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;14.jpg&#34; title=&#34;14.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TCL么么哒3N 还有一个很不错的功能——么么哒 2.0，利用它可以实现手机与手机、手机与电脑间的文件零流量互传。这个软件的名字和手机一样也叫“么么哒”，也许这就是这部手机名字的由来。只需要把两 台装有么么哒应用的手机处于同一网段下，即可完成数据互传，支持任何类型的文件，连已经安装好的应用都可以传输。摆脱了数据线的束缚，对于我们这些懒人来 说，再实用不过了。此外，么么哒 2.0还支持与苹果设备和电脑设备相连。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143508baw9h0whnj2kroah.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;18.jpg&#34; title=&#34;18.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TCL么么哒3N 自带了安全中心，提供病毒防护，安全阻拦、垃圾清理、自启管理、通知管理等功能，一次性的为用户解决杂乱无章的App问题。此外，还提供了省电管理系统， 可以自动执行智能省电功能，在夜晚睡眠的时候最好用，在大容量电池的同时拥有不错的省电系统，可以为我们带来更久的续航体验。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143533blmvvmljm37v5jlf.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;19.jpg&#34; title=&#34;19.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;其实TCL么么哒3N 还带来了非常多不错的小功能，比如：色温调节可以让我们无惧冷暖屏，短信图标因为有短信，偶尔会像果冻一样蠕动。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143601gqfxim7iie77r9wc.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;20.jpg&#34; title=&#34;20.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;性能 · 八核强劲续航给力：&lt;/strong&gt; 硬件实力对千元机来说是一个非常重要的功能点，低廉的售价下要拥有不错的性能，幸亏有了联发科来解决这件事情。TCL么么哒3N 虽然没有骁龙805等豪华硬件，但从屏幕、处理器、内存到存储方面均有升级。TCL么么哒3N 搭载一颗64位联发科MT6752八核处理器，主频最高可达1.7GHz。运行内存升级至2GB、机身存储空间也是提升到了16GB。对于这个价格配置相 当不错，保证系统流畅运行之余，还未多任务处理预留足够的存储空间。从实际跑分表现来看，还真的让我感到一些吃惊，安兔兔达到了40000+的高分。 &lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143440l17u5u4swohor3ss.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;17.jpg&#34; title=&#34;17.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;在这些跑分数据之外，我也拿着TCL么么哒3N 进行了几款游戏的试用，运行《狂野飙车8》还是非常流畅，途中也没有出现闪退、屏幕拖影等情况。不过当我试玩捕鱼达人3时，后面的壁纸全部黑屏了，出现了BUG，联发科处理器在部分游戏上兼容性还是有问题的。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/143413w2eqvq7c2w2ek21e.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;16.jpg&#34; title=&#34;16.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;续航方面，TCL么么哒3 N内置了一枚3500mAh电池，这个容量已经超越了现在大多千元机水准，很多旗舰机也没有这大。时间使用中，日常使用2天应该是没有多少问题的。&lt;strong&gt;拍照 · 白天尚可夜间加油：&lt;/strong&gt;TCL么么哒3N 采用800W像素的前置摄像头和索尼1300W像素IMX214堆栈式后置摄像头，拍摄界面，除了常见的滤镜效果、HDR、全景效果外，还可以手动调节曝光补偿、白平衡等参数、界面看起来有些老旧，未来可以在设计上多下功夫。 &lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152224jvgu9gixu1qxxuqb.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;31.jpg&#34; title=&#34;31.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/151912rnhe2f3qienh37f7.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;25.jpg&#34; title=&#34;25.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TCL么么哒3N 在白天的成像效果还不错，照片整体的饱和度不错，色彩还原也比较真实，部分场景在光线差异较大的情况会出现涂抹的问题，大场景的白平衡控制尚算不错。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/151848n1m6zmyr9d7qmmk1.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;24.jpg&#34; title=&#34;24.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/151941ppp0vhfqo7gyloc0.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;26.jpg&#34; title=&#34;26.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;微距下对焦速度会显得偏慢，并且偶尔出现对焦不准的情况，当然肯定要比599的联想乐檬好的多。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152330q4txomtgxcxxcfct.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;27_副本.jpg&#34; title=&#34;27_副本.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152142ug9ccr4rb6hjrgr4.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;28.jpg&#34; title=&#34;28.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;在拍摄静物时，可以看到画质的解析度相当不错，色彩表现比较真实，还原度较高，看上去也比较丰满，照片颜色和曝光度都恰到好处。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152204p6u42dp69j44huux.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;30.jpg&#34; title=&#34;30.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152116u9mehf9v2raumroa.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;29.jpg&#34; title=&#34;29.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;夜景噪点控制以及色彩的还原缺了些许火候，噪点抑制以及放眩光方面还需继续加强。&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/150627ap5fgp46k9agi9iu.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;23.jpg&#34; title=&#34;23.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;自拍方面，前置摄像头高达800W像素，可以拍出高质量的自拍照，配合美颜功能，还不错。&lt;strong&gt;总结 · 虽有不足依然实惠：&lt;/strong&gt;综合来看，TCL么么哒3N 确实可以说给千元机硬件上树立了一个新的标杆。设计上么么哒3N还是属于比较保守的设计，但是融入了时尚的色彩搭配，让整机机器不至于廉价。系统虽然给人 印象一般，但还是非常实在、实用的。硬件上采用了高清1080屏、八核64位处理器、4G网络、1300W像素索尼IMX214摄像头等都给TCL么么哒 3N 加分不少。也有非常有趣的么么哒2.0 让我们拥有了更简单的传输方式。当然TCL么么哒3N 还有很多问题，比如：卡槽位置设计太深以及拍照成像欠缺，这些虽然说问题不大，但是还需要引起重视。这样一款售价不足千元的手机，的确是对得起它的价格， 对一款千元机的要求我们不必过分吹毛求疵了，不然要高端机干嘛？对吧。 &lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152313vkqnsrd11ozvvrqn.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;33.jpg&#34; title=&#34;33.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://img.dgtle.com/forum/201412/31/152244w8n3e8dm5nve85g8.jpg%21680px&#34; alt=&#34;32.jpg&#34; title=&#34;32.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;优点：&lt;/strong&gt; 5.5英寸1080P屏幕 双卡槽都支持4G 2G内存，16G存储 3500mAh电池&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;缺点：&lt;/strong&gt; 联发科处理器兼容性一般 卡槽位置太深，不容易取换 系统体验欠佳 拍照不理想&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;p&gt;by &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/author/637681&#34;&gt;maomaobear&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/8520cc3bc0a952ed24958ef3ba47c7e0_w_680_h_425.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A while ago Tencent did a survey on wearable devices, with a sample size of 24,877 and with weighting applied, so its credibility is quite high. The data revealed some very interesting phenomena. Let’s take a look.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;1-Wearable-devices-much-thunder-little-rain&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#1-Wearable-devices-much-thunder-little-rain&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;1. Wearable devices: much thunder, little rain&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;1. Wearable devices: much thunder, little rain&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The data shows that among the internet population, a great many people know about wearable devices, but only 2.9% are willing to use one, which is a fairly low proportion. On the one hand this shows that the market still has great potential; on the other hand, it shows that today’s wearable devices have not yet found people’s real pain points, and too few people can actually make use of them.&lt;span id=&#34;more&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/d8b02a85f7fff3856b9dad807b6d0469_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report - 1.jpg&#34; title=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt; As for the types used, people still use whatever they can buy. And they are closely tied to phones. Smart glasses are all the rage, but you cannot buy them. Samsung’s smart watch and Xiaomi’s smart band are sold alongside phones, so it is very convenient for users to add some money and pick one up. So these two still hold a numerical advantage. &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/2d6f787aa177215c3ac1e15c824e7891_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report - 2.jpg&#34; title=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/62a7e2da310bdb98fb0b60102a6876e2_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report - 3.jpg&#34; title=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;2-Trying-something-new-—-novelty-is-the-selling-point&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#2-Trying-something-new-—-novelty-is-the-selling-point&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;2. Trying something new — novelty is the selling point&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;2. Trying something new — novelty is the selling point&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/0631ba089fcd29d70c2e3d2ae75f7cc9_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report - 4.jpg&#34; title=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt; Looking at the channels through which people learn about them, tech websites are the main channel through which users hear about wearable devices, followed by product official sites and shopping sites. Online media, especially specialist media, play an important role in promoting wearable devices. &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/aa3f874fb850d8908be9af3a69af4289_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report - 5.jpg&#34; title=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt; I did the maths on the proportion of users who bought one themselves: about three quarters paid out of their own pocket. Adding in the 2.9% usage rate from above, only 2.17% of users actually paid money for a wearable device. In terms of channels, official sites and physical stores are also important channels for phone purchases, which shows that wearable devices are currently very closely tied to smartphones. &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/4223a1d5b9e017dda51515829140e5d2_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report - 6.jpg&#34; title=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt; The product usage rate is pitiful too: 58% of people are still using theirs, and the rest have basically given up, which shows that fitness bands are not very practical and that quite a few get thrown aside after the novelty wears off. &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/5bb77e5c6d452aee283844d47756dc05_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report - 7.jpg&#34; title=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt; The satisfaction rate is about the same as the still-using rate. Too few functions, poor battery life and the hassle of connecting to a phone are the three main reasons. A poor experience and not being of much use are the main problems with wearable devices. From this data, wearable devices are still at the toy stage: people see them introduced in the tech media, pick one up along with a phone purchase to play with, and stop using it once it turns out not to be much good. A product that truly hits a pain point and is widely accepted has yet to appear.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;3-Who-is-using-wearable-devices&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#3-Who-is-using-wearable-devices&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;3. Who is using wearable devices?&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;3. Who is using wearable devices?&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/b443471216b517cc30cb9eea354e023d_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report - 8.jpg&#34; title=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/6003950cffdc86970909a494861920c6_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report - 9.jpg&#34; title=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/7db181be25ab69447b69a185006d9b03_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report - 10.jpg&#34; title=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/07d34e2419c61216a85a2156b2cf8ae4_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report - 11.jpg&#34; title=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/b5f30ed55c1e0b0c8be8d25edacb6f94_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report - 12.jpg&#34; title=&#34;Still Just a Toy for Now — An Analysis of the Wearable Device Report&#34;&gt; There is a very interesting figure in the survey: students make up 20% of users, and 18.1% were unwilling to disclose their income. Students with no income account for no small share of wearable device users. Looking at the groups, people with an education from junior high school up to university, and the backbone of society aged 20-40, are also the main force consuming wearable devices. Wearable devices are gladly accepted by the backbone of society, but that shows their potential; the fact that they are not yet widespread is a problem with the products themselves, not with the users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;4-Conclusion&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#4-Conclusion&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;4. Conclusion&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;4. Conclusion&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Judging from Tencent’s survey results, wearable devices are already recognised by netizens and have very high awareness among the mainstream population. They have great market potential, but since current products do not have sufficiently attractive features and the experience is not good either, people’s satisfaction and desire to buy are both fairly low, and they remain at the toy stage. There is still a long way to go from potential to sales. From www.zoopda.com/2719&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;p&gt;by &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/author/637681&#34;&gt;maomaobear&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/8520cc3bc0a952ed24958ef3ba47c7e0_w_680_h_425.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;日前，腾讯对穿戴式设备做了一个调查，样本数量达到了 24877 个，而且做了配比处理，可信度颇高。数据显示了一些很有意思的现象，我们来看一下。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;一、穿戴式设备雷声大雨点小&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#一、穿戴式设备雷声大雨点小&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;一、穿戴式设备雷声大雨点小&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;一、穿戴式设备雷声大雨点小&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;数据现实，在互联网群体中，知道穿戴式设备的人还是很多的，但是肯使用的只有 2.9% 了，这个比例还是比较低的。一方面说明这个市场的潜力还很大，另外一方面，说明现在的穿戴式设备还没有找到人们的需求痛点，能用到的人太少。&lt;span id=&#34;more&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/d8b02a85f7fff3856b9dad807b6d0469_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析 - 1.jpg&#34; title=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt; 从使用的种类看，还是什么能买到就用什么。而且和手机密切相关。智能眼睛很热闹，买不到啊。三星的智能手表，小米的智能手环跟着手机卖，用户加钱拿一个很方便。所以这两种还是占数量优势。 &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/2d6f787aa177215c3ac1e15c824e7891_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析 - 2.jpg&#34; title=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/62a7e2da310bdb98fb0b60102a6876e2_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析 - 3.jpg&#34; title=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;二、尝鲜，新奇是卖点&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#二、尝鲜，新奇是卖点&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;二、尝鲜，新奇是卖点&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;二、尝鲜，新奇是卖点&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/0631ba089fcd29d70c2e3d2ae75f7cc9_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析 - 4.jpg&#34; title=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt; 从获知渠道看，科技网站是用户知道穿戴式设备的主要渠道，然后是产品官网和购物网站，网络媒体，特别是专业媒体对于穿戴式设备的宣传有重要作用。 &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/aa3f874fb850d8908be9af3a69af4289_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析 - 5.jpg&#34; title=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt; 算了一下用户自己购买的比率，大约有四分之三是自己掏钱的，如果算上前面 2.9% 的使用率，只有 2.17% 的用户掏钱买了穿戴式设备。从渠道看，官网和实体店也是手机购买的重要渠道，说明穿戴式设备目前和智能手机的关系很密切。 &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/4223a1d5b9e017dda51515829140e5d2_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析 - 6.jpg&#34; title=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt; 产品使用率也很可怜，有 58% 的人还在用，其余基本放弃，说明手环的实用性不高，尝鲜过后扔掉的不少。 &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/5bb77e5c6d452aee283844d47756dc05_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析 - 7.jpg&#34; title=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt; 满意率和还在用的比例差不多，功能太少，电池续航差，连接手机麻烦是三大原因。体验差，没啥用是穿戴式设备的主要问题。 从这些数据看，穿戴式设备还在玩具阶段，大家看到科技媒体介绍，买手机的时候顺便拿来玩玩，用用不好用就不玩了。真正找到痛点被广泛接受的产品还没出现。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;三、什么人在用穿戴式设备？&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#三、什么人在用穿戴式设备？&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;三、什么人在用穿戴式设备？&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;三、什么人在用穿戴式设备？&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/b443471216b517cc30cb9eea354e023d_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析 - 8.jpg&#34; title=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/6003950cffdc86970909a494861920c6_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析 - 9.jpg&#34; title=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/7db181be25ab69447b69a185006d9b03_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析 - 10.jpg&#34; title=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/07d34e2419c61216a85a2156b2cf8ae4_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析 - 11.jpg&#34; title=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt; &lt;img src=&#34;http://www.zoopda.com/thumbs/2014/12/24/b5f30ed55c1e0b0c8be8d25edacb6f94_mw_680_wm_0_wmp_3.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析 - 12.jpg&#34; title=&#34;目前还是玩物——可穿戴式设备报告解析&#34;&gt; 调查里面有个很有意思的数字，学生比例是 20%，收入不愿意透露是 18.1%。无收入的学生在穿戴式设备中占得比例并不小。 从人群看，初中到大学文化，20-40 岁的社会中坚力量也是穿戴式设备消费的主力军。 穿戴式设备乐于被社会中坚力量所接受，但是这表明了它的潜力，而目前没有普及，是产品本身的问题，而非用户的问题。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;四、结论&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#四、结论&#34; class=&#34;headerlink&#34; title=&#34;四、结论&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;四、结论&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;从腾讯的调查结果看，穿戴式设备已经被网民认知，在主流人群中有很高的认知普及。有很大的市场潜力，但是由于目前的产品没有足够诱人的功能，体验也不好。人们对其满意度和购买欲望都是比较低的，还停留在玩具的阶段。从潜力到销量还有很长的路要走。出自www.zoopda.com/2719&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;p&gt;12月8日消息，亚马逊集团董事会主席兼CEO杰夫·贝佐斯(Jeff Bezos)表示，亚马逊将会发布更多款的智能手机。外界希望他能从亚马逊Fire Phone的惨痛失败中接受教训并汲取经验。这款手机的失败导致亚马逊从众多手机制造商中脱颖而出的想法变得愈加难以实现。 关于亚马逊的Fire Phone，有两点值得注意。&lt;span id=&#34;more&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;第一，它仅在美国发售；&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;第二，顾客只能购买SIM-free非定制机（这在欧洲市场并不适用）或者是美国电话电报公司 （AT&amp;amp;T）的合约机。如Facebook与HTC联合推出的手机HTC First一样，如果Fire Phone能在网上热销，那一定会震惊许多人。 但Fire Phone有一个优势：亚马逊首页是全球最大的互联网购物窗口之一，Fire Phone有它作为支撑。亚马逊的全部商品分类中可以将Fire Phone放在任意位置，以吸引潜在客户。 如人们所料，亚马逊并未公布Fire Phone相关的销售数据，但有两点可以提示Fire Phone属于“失败产品”的行列。第一点是合约机价格急剧下降（目前两年合约价为99美分），第二点是亚马逊在有关该款手机的成本记录上显示公司减记1.7亿美元。 但杰夫·贝佐斯仍坚持Fire Phone的项目。他表示，在最终确定该项目成功与否之前，“它需要经历几次迭代”。 但笔者对此持不同观点。消费者对商家的信赖需要很长时间才能建立，亚马逊最初冒险尝试Kindle电子书阅读器以及随后的Kindle Fire平板都耗费了好几年时间以取得消费者对亚马逊的信任。但Fire Phone的质量将这份信任迅速消耗，并且没有挽回的可能。 对当今的智能手机制造商而言，市场份额的丢失可以快得出奇，并且是灾难性的。悬崖理论表明一旦消费者的信任不在，那么对手机制造商的支持就会急剧下降，并 且无法挽回。诺基亚，Palm，爱立信（ Ericsson），西门子，飞利浦(Phillips)以及很多其他的公司都曾在此败倒，三星目前似乎也正在接近这个结局。亚马逊在发售Fire Phone前不曾建立起一个强大的智能手机市场，因此它也不存在丢失大份额市场的问题，对它而言，问题在于也许根本无法起步。 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;当Fire Phone2 面世时，它将与Kindle Fire占有相同的市场份额，但会有更多的消费者带着怀疑与谨慎的目光对Fire Phone2进行审视。这并不单单是艰难的第二版的发售，还需要克服一大堆消极思想的包袱。 笔者没有理由质疑贝佐斯坚持开发Fire Phone以期它能进入正轨的行为，因此为了使Fire Phone2 有希望被市场接受，我强调以下三点： &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;拓宽运营商网络&lt;/strong&gt; 撇开SIM-free非定制机不说，与AT&amp;amp;T制定合约机严重限制了Fire Phone的吸引力。消费者不仅需要一个Fire Phone，还需要与AT&amp;amp;T签订合同，并随着该网络的更新而更新，或者是违约才能使用其他的。这是很多人都关心的问题。大规模销售需要减少消费 者购买的障碍，而与AT&amp;amp;T合作使之独家销售可能会给亚马逊减少一些广告和制造费用，我怀疑AT&amp;amp;T是否帮亚马逊支付了那1.7亿美元的 减记。 Fire Phone 的销售需要全美网络的支持，但这并不意味着它就应该局限于美国境内。世界是相互连通的，美国之外的那些想要Fire Phone的智能手机粉丝们也应该是该手机的潜在客户。亚马逊需要拓展市场，并且在新机发布时（或之后几周内）就让这些地方的客户能够购买到。 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;做到物有所值甚至超值&lt;/strong&gt; 物有所值并不仅仅意味着低价。亚马逊不可能把这款手机在美国的价格降至低于99美分，而且购买该手机即享受亚马逊金牌会员1年的优惠也着实诱人。但该款手机并没有兑现它们“做一款好手机”的诺言。点评说这款手机音质差，相机功能不行，以及用户界面不佳。 《福布斯》杂志的Ian Morris指出：“和Fire平板相似，Fire Phone的界面也是一团糟。这确实是个问题，因为如果消费者们对手机性能不满而不愿购买，那么手机很难销售出去。苹果的iPhone之所以畅销就是因为 无论是谁拿起手机，都能够进行操作。我是一位经验丰富的科技行业记者，对我而言，Fire Phone的用户界面的确不怎么样。”‍ 如果消费者们买到的东西毫无用处，那么就这个东西是否便宜对他们而言就没有太大意义了。 亚马逊需要下更大的功夫，让Fire Phone成为一流产品，与其他智能手机相比时能更胜一筹。为了能与现在的知名品牌相媲美，Fire Phone需要做到更好、更快、更流畅，超过其他职能手机如Galaxy S5、iPhone6等。 另外，这款SIM-free非定制机应对得起450美元的价格。然而，亚马逊现在尚未达到这个标准。 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;增强手机的兼容性与实用性&lt;/strong&gt; 表面上看来，Fire Phone搭载了安卓系统是一个好消息。安卓系统是消费者们熟知的，它拥有消费者的信任，而且它在业界中也算是一个标志性的操作系统。 当然，这并不是谷歌版本的安卓系统，而是亚马逊版本的。通过改进了Android开放源 项目，亚马逊已经拥有了一套稳定的现代操作系统供其运行。但这个操作系统却没有与Google Play、Google Play Services以及谷歌的首批应用Gmail或谷歌地图等形成连接。然而，这些应用恰恰是诸多消费者十分依赖的。 消费者们已经购买过的那些安卓应用呢？他们需要在亚马逊上重新购买，而不是重新安装即可的。这样的话Fire Phone的App Store上应该拥有所有消费者想要的软件，但事实并不是这样。 亚马逊需要快速而高效地解决这个问题，并且需要在时间和金钱上都付出巨大代价。 如果没有好的主意，软件效用上以及应用兼容方面的缺陷将会使消费者们远离Fire Phone。 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;其他措施&lt;/strong&gt; 较差的性能与业界对Fire Phone的差评让亚马逊在智能手机市场举步维艰，很难获得成功。Fire Phone2需要从亚马逊、各个运营商、业内分析师以及消费者那里获得更多的支持。 正如苹果当初发售iPhone的时候一样，Fire Phone的团队应该与多家运营商洽谈，而不是从某一家做起或者打压另一家。他们需要更具战略性，建立更多的合作伙伴及合作关系，并关注现实世界中消费者对于Fire Phone设计改进的反响。 值得庆幸的是，贝佐斯并未放弃。但我想看到的不止是产品的迭代以及配置的优化。要达到预期的销售量，Fire Phone2得下很大功夫。价格、效用以及资金价值方面都需要改进。‍ 本文作者为福布斯专栏作家伊万-斯宾塞。&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;p&gt;News from December 8: Amazon chairman and CEO Jeff Bezos says Amazon will release more smartphones. The outside world hopes he has taken the lessons of the Fire Phone’s painful failure to heart. That failure has made Amazon’s ambition of standing out from the crowd of phone makers harder and harder to realize. There are two things worth noting about the Amazon Fire Phone.&lt;span id=&#34;more&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;First, it was only sold in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Second, customers could only buy the SIM-free unlocked version (which doesn’t apply in the European market) or a contract phone from AT&amp;amp;T. Just like the HTC First that Facebook and HTC launched together, if the Fire Phone had sold well online, it would have astonished plenty of people. But the Fire Phone had one advantage: Amazon’s homepage is one of the largest internet shopping windows in the world, and the Fire Phone had that behind it. Amazon could place the Fire Phone anywhere it liked among its product categories to draw in potential customers. As expected, Amazon did not publish any Fire Phone sales data, but two things hint that the Fire Phone belongs in the “failed product” column. The first is the sharp drop in the contract price (the two-year contract price is now 99 cents), and the second is that Amazon’s cost records for the phone show a $170 million writedown. Yet Jeff Bezos still stuck with the Fire Phone project. He said that before it can finally be judged a success or a failure, “it needs to go through several iterations.” But this writer takes a different view. Consumer trust in a seller takes a long time to build, and Amazon’s early gamble on the Kindle e-reader, followed by the Kindle Fire tablet, took several years to earn consumers’ trust. But the quality of the Fire Phone burned through that trust fast, with no chance of winning it back. For today’s smartphone makers, market share can be lost startlingly fast, and catastrophically. The cliff theory holds that once consumer trust is gone, support for a phone maker plunges and cannot be recovered. Nokia, Palm, Ericsson, Siemens, Philips and many other companies have fallen this way, and Samsung now seems to be approaching that same ending. Amazon never built a strong smartphone market before launching the Fire Phone, so it doesn’t have a large market share to lose — its problem is that it may never get off the ground at all.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When the Fire Phone 2 arrives, it will hold the same market share as the Kindle Fire, but even more consumers will scrutinize the Fire Phone 2 with doubt and caution. This is not simply a difficult second-version launch; it also has to overcome a whole baggage load of negativity. This writer has no reason to question Bezos’s insistence on developing the Fire Phone in the hope that it will get back on track, so for the Fire Phone 2 to have any hope of being accepted by the market, I want to stress the following three points:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Broaden the carrier network.&lt;/strong&gt; Setting aside the SIM-free unlocked model, tying the phone to an AT&amp;amp;T contract severely limited the Fire Phone’s appeal. Consumers not only need a Fire Phone, they also need to sign a contract with AT&amp;amp;T and keep up with that network’s updates — or break the contract — in order to use another one. This is a concern for a lot of people. Selling at scale requires lowering the barriers to purchase, and partnering with AT&amp;amp;T for exclusive sales may have saved Amazon some advertising and manufacturing costs; I suspect AT&amp;amp;T helped Amazon pay for that $170 million writedown. Fire Phone sales need the support of networks across the whole United States, but that doesn’t mean it should be limited to US soil. The world is interconnected, and the smartphone fans outside the US who want a Fire Phone should also be potential customers. Amazon needs to expand its market and make the phone available to customers in those places at launch (or within a few weeks after).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver good value for money, or even more.&lt;/strong&gt; Value for money doesn’t just mean a low price. Amazon can’t push the US price of this phone below 99 cents, and the one-year Amazon Prime membership bundled with the purchase is genuinely tempting. But the phone didn’t deliver on its promise of “making a good phone.” Reviews say the phone has poor sound quality, a subpar camera and an awkward user interface. Ian Morris of Forbes magazine pointed out: “Like the Fire tablet, the Fire Phone’s interface is a mess. That really is a problem, because if consumers are unhappy with the phone’s performance and don’t want to buy it, then the phone is hard to sell. Apple’s iPhone sells well because no matter who picks up the phone, they can use it. I’m an experienced tech industry journalist, and for me the Fire Phone’s user interface really isn’t up to much.” If what consumers buy is useless, then how cheap it is doesn’t mean much to them. Amazon needs to put in much more effort to make the Fire Phone a first-class product that comes out ahead of other smartphones. To stand alongside today’s well-known brands, the Fire Phone needs to be better, faster and smoother than other smartphones such as the Galaxy S5 and the iPhone 6. In addition, this SIM-free unlocked model should be worth its $450 price. However, Amazon has not yet reached that standard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve the phone’s compatibility and usefulness.&lt;/strong&gt; On the face of it, the Fire Phone running Android is good news. Android is familiar to consumers, it has their trust, and it counts as a flagship operating system in the industry. Of course, this isn’t Google’s version of Android, it’s Amazon’s. By improving the Android Open Source Project, Amazon already has a stable, modern operating system for it to run on. But that operating system has no connection to Google Play, Google Play Services, or Google’s first-party apps like Gmail or Google Maps. Yet these are exactly the apps many consumers depend on. What about the Android apps consumers have already bought? They would need to buy them again on Amazon rather than simply reinstalling them. That being the case, the Fire Phone’s App Store should have every piece of software consumers want, but the fact is it doesn’t. Amazon needs to solve this problem quickly and efficiently, and it will have to pay a steep price in both time and money. Without a good idea, gaps in software usability and app compatibility will drive consumers away from the Fire Phone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other measures.&lt;/strong&gt; Poor performance and the industry’s negative reviews of the Fire Phone leave Amazon struggling in the smartphone market, with little chance of success. The Fire Phone 2 needs more support from Amazon, the carriers, industry analysts and consumers. Just as Apple did when it launched the iPhone, the Fire Phone team should talk to multiple carriers rather than starting with one or squeezing out another. They need to be more strategic, build more partners and partnerships, and pay attention to how consumers in the real world respond to improvements in the Fire Phone’s design. Fortunately, Bezos hasn’t given up. But I want to see more than product iterations and spec improvements. To hit its expected sales figures, the Fire Phone 2 has a lot of work to do. Price, usefulness and value for money all need improvement. The author of this article is Forbes columnist Ewan Spence.&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Horizontal Partitioning&lt;/strong&gt; What is horizontal partitioning? A rather vivid analogy: when you eat in a canteen there is only one window, and the queue for food gets so long that it coils into an S shape, which easily makes the people in line anxious and prone to chaos. Then a manager steps up, adds several more serving windows, and cuts that long queue in half into several lines. To put it even more vividly: you take a “scalpel” and slash a big table a few times, and the big table turns into several small tables. Horizontal partitioning places data into two or more independent tables according to certain conditions. That is, it partitions by records — different records can be stored separately, and each sub-table has the same number of columns. Horizontal splitting divides a table into multiple tables. Each table contains the same number of columns, but fewer data rows.&lt;span id=&#34;more&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;For example, a table containing a billion rows can be horizontally partitioned into 12 tables, each small table representing one month of data in a specific year. Any query that needs data for a particular month only has to reference the table for that month. The conditions usually used to horizontally partition a table include: the date-time dimension, the region dimension, and so on — and of course more business dimensions. Let me give a few examples to explain: Case 1: A company’s sales record data volume is too large, so we can horizontally partition it by month, with each month’s sales records in a separate table. Case 2: A group has branch companies in various regions, and the group’s order data table is too large, so we can horizontally split it by the region where each branch is located. Case 3: A telecom company’s call detail records, after being horizontally split by date and city, were found to still have too much data, so they then split them horizontally by brand and number segment. Horizontal partitioning is usually used in the following situations: (1)    The table has a very large volume of data; after splitting, the data and index pages that must be read during a query are reduced, and the number of index levels is lowered as well, speeding up queries. (2)    The data in the table is inherently independent — for example, the table records data for each region or data for different periods separately, especially when some data is used often and some is not. (3)    The data needs to be stored on multiple media. (4)    Historical data and current data need to be separated. Advantages: 1: It reduces the data and index pages that must be read during a query, and also lowers the number of index levels, speeding up queries. Disadvantages: 1: Horizontal partitioning adds complexity to the application; queries usually need multiple table names, and querying all the data requires a union operation. In many database applications this complexity outweighs the benefits it brings, because as long as the index key isn’t large, when the index is used for queries and the table gains two to three times more data, a query only adds one more disk read of an index level. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Vertical Partitioning&lt;/strong&gt; What is vertical partitioning? A vivid analogy: a small company grows into a large multinational enterprise in just a few short years, and its old departmental structure clearly can no longer satisfy the current business growth, so the CEO splits the company into a finance department, an HR department, a production department, a sales department….. setting up many departments at once, each with its own duties. That analogy is fairly apt, isn’t it? Hehe. When you vertically partition a table (without breaking third normal form), you put the primary key and some columns into one table, then put the primary key and some other columns into another table. The original table is split into multiple tables that each contain fewer columns. If some columns in a table are used often and other columns are not, vertical partitioning can be applied. Advantages: 1: Vertical partitioning makes the row data smaller, so a single data block (Block) can hold more data, which reduces the number of I/Os during queries (fewer Blocks are read per query). 2: Vertical partitioning a table achieves maximum use of the Cache. Disadvantages: 1: After vertical partitioning, the primary key becomes redundant, and the redundant columns need to be managed. 2: It gives rise to table JOIN operations (increasing CPU overhead), which needs to be avoided at the business level. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Table Sharding&lt;/strong&gt; Table sharding is similar to horizontal partitioning, but without as clear a dividing line as horizontal partitioning; a Hash algorithm is used to spread the data across the shard tables, so that the IO is more balanced. Generally speaking, we separate databases by business or functional module, with different modules corresponding to different databases or tables, and then apply a certain strategy to further shard a page or function at a smaller database level — for example, the user table sharded by user ID into 128 tables, which should be able to improve system performance at low cost and offers good scalability. Reference: &lt;a href=&#34;http://blog.csdn.net/tianlesoftware/article/details/7674501&#34;&gt;http://blog.csdn.net/tianlesoftware/article/details/7674501&lt;/a&gt; Original article address: &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.cnblogs.com/kerrycode/archive/2013/01/25/2876195.html&#34;&gt;http://www.cnblogs.com/kerrycode/archive/2013/01/25/2876195.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;一．水平分割&lt;/strong&gt; 什么是水平分割？打个比较形象的比喻，在食堂吃 饭的时候，只有一个窗口，排队打饭的队伍太长了，都排成S型了，这时容易让排队的人产生焦虑情绪，容易产生混乱，这时一个管理者站出来，增加多个打饭窗 口，把那条长长的队伍拦腰截断成几队。更形象一点的理解，你拿一把“手术刀”，把一个大表猛的切了几刀，结果这个大表，变成了几个小表. 水平分割根据某些条件将数据放到两个或多个独立 的表中。即按记录进分分割，不同的记录可以分开保存，每个子表的列数相同。水平切割将表分为多个表。每个表包含的列数相同，但是数据行更少。&lt;span id=&#34;more&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;例如，可以将 一个包含十亿行的表水平分区成 12 个表，每个小表表示特定年份内一个月的数据。任何需要特定月份数据的查询只需引用相应月份的表。 通常用来水平分割表的条件有：日期时间维度、地区维度等，当然还有更多的业务维度。下面我举几个例子来解说一下 案例1：某个公司销售记录数据量太大了，我们可以对它按月进行水平分割，每个月的销售记录单独成一张表。 案例2：某个集团在各个地区都有分公司，该集团的订单数据表太大了，我们可以按分公司所在的地区进行水平切割。 案例3：某电信公司的话单按日期、地市水平切割后，发现数据量太大，然后他们又按品牌、号码段进行水平切割 水平分割通常在下面的情况下使用： （1）    表数据量很大，分割后可以降低在查询时需要读的数据和索引的页数，同时也降低了索引的层数，加快了查询速度。 （2）    表中的数据本来就有独立性，例如表中分别记录各个地区的数据或不同时期的数据，特别是有些数据常用，而另外一些数据不常用。 （3）    需要把数据存放到多个介质上。 （4）    需要把历史数据和当前的数据拆分开。 优点： 1：降低在查询时需要读的数据和索引的页数，同时也降低了索引的层数，加快了查询速度。 缺点： 1：水平分割会给应用增加复杂度，它通常在查询时需要多个表名，查询所有数据需要union操作。在许多数据库应用中，这种复杂性会超过它带来的优点，因为只要索引关键字不大，则在索引用于查询时，表中增加两到三倍数据量，查询时也就增加读一个索引层的磁盘次数。 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;二．垂直分割&lt;/strong&gt; 什么是垂直分割呢？打个形象的比喻，一个小公司 通过短短几年发展变成了一个跨国大企业，以前的部门架构明显不能满足现在的业务发展，CEO噼里啪啦的把公司分成了财务部、人事部、生产部、销售部 门…..，一下子成立了多个部门，各司其职。这个还算比较形象吧，有木有？呵呵 你垂直分割表（不破坏第三范式），把主码(主键)和一些列放到一个表，然后把主码(主键)和另外的一些列放到另一个表中。将原始表分成多个只包含较少列的表。如果一个表中某些列常用，而另外一些列不常用，则可以采用垂直分割。 优点： 1：垂直分割可以使得行数据变小，一个数据块(Block)就能存放更多的数据，在查询时就会减少I/O次数(每次查询时读取的Block 就少)。 2：垂直分割表可以达到最大化利用Cache的目的。 缺点： 1：表垂直分割后，主码(主键)出现冗余，需要管理冗余列 2：会引起表连接JOIN操作（增加CPU开销）需要从业务上规避 &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;三. 库表散列&lt;/strong&gt; 表散列与水平分割相似，但没有水平分割那样的明显分割界限，采用Hash算法把数据分散到各个分表中, 这样IO更加均衡。一般来说，我们会按照业务或者功能模块将数据库进行分离，不同的模块对应不同的数据库或者表，再按照一定的策略对某个页面或者功能进行 更小的数据库散列，比如用户表，按照用户ID进行表散列，散列128张表，则应就能够低成本的提升系统的性能并且有很好的扩展性 参考资料：&lt;a href=&#34;http://blog.csdn.net/tianlesoftware/article/details/7674501&#34;&gt;http://blog.csdn.net/tianlesoftware/article/details/7674501&lt;/a&gt; 原始文章地址：&lt;a href=&#34;http://www.cnblogs.com/kerrycode/archive/2013/01/25/2876195.html&#34;&gt;http://www.cnblogs.com/kerrycode/archive/2013/01/25/2876195.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
